                            <comment id="16017614" author="githubbot" created="Fri, 19 May 2017 16:20:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user felixcheung commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2347&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2347&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Perhaps multiple queries was the reason we tried to parse the text (we really need to document these things better) - though I&apos;m not sure how it would work exactly? Do you get multiple table in result if there are multiple queries in one paragraph? Does it even handle the multiple results correctly since that was added after JDBC interpreter is implemented?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    In any case I do think it is much cleaner not to mess with the content.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Perhaps default to single query with a switch to fallback to old code and see if we get any feedback on this.&lt;/p&gt;

</comment>
                            <comment id="16017695" author="githubbot" created="Fri, 19 May 2017 17:22:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user prabhjyotsingh commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

